WEBVTT

00:00:02.930 --> 00:00:04.940
I’m going to become a nurse!

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:07.690
Why such a sudden change of heart?

00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:11.410
I’m bad at whatever I do.

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:15.660
For me, becoming a nurse might be impossible.

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:19.460
But, I...

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:23.580
I want to become a wife fit for Irie-kun!

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:27.760
You, a nurse? Think about the patients who have to be treated by you!

00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:32.140
Why not?

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:38.890
You should try.

00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:49.240
And with that, I’m now running towards a new dream of becoming a nurse.

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:51.570
Or maybe not.

00:00:51.910 --> 00:00:54.160
Oh my God!

00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:57.450
For some reason, I failed.

00:00:58.790 --> 00:01:01.250
Could this be...

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:06.340
...someone’s conspiracy to break Irie-kun and me up?

00:01:06.340 --> 00:01:10.840
Or is this a marital test of love from God?

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:15.050
However!

00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:19.140
I won’t be beaten by something like that!

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:22.150
Anyway, this year I will pass the transfer examinations

00:01:22.150 --> 00:01:25.430
and walk the path towards becoming a nurse!

00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:28.850
What are you getting all excited about?

00:01:29.190 --> 00:01:31.610
Sheesh, do you want to fail again this year?

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:34.160
Well, I’ll be fine.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:38.160
Because, this year, if I pass, you’ll reward me with a date.

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:40.450
What the heck is that?

00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:42.200
Who said such a thing?

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:47.460
Well, I think I’ll be able to study better with something like that.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:49.580
I’m doing this for your sake, you know.

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:53.970
If it weren’t for stuff like this, you’d never go on a proper date with me!

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:57.390
Fine then.

00:01:57.390 --> 00:01:58.600
Really?!

00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:00.680
I’ll work hard then!

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:01.970
Sure, sure.

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:35.440
You may begin.

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:46.870
Finally finished.

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:49.120
It should turn out well this year.

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:50.910
It’ll turn out fine, Kotoko.

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:52.790
I’m sure you’ll pass.

00:03:53.290 --> 00:03:56.000
You’re right. Thank you, Chris!

00:03:59.630 --> 00:04:04.300
I’ve gotta pass this year so I can get a date from Irie-kun!

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:06.550
Oh, a date?

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:09.050
Kinnosuke, why don’t we go on a date too?

00:04:09.050 --> 00:04:11.470
Huh? What are you saying?

00:04:11.470 --> 00:04:15.350
Watching a movie with you, then having a meal together...

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:17.940
Be quiet! I’m working!

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:20.320
Come on. Let’s have a date.

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:24.070
Looks like you’re becoming more and more like Kin-chan, Chris.

00:04:24.070 --> 00:04:27.950
I have fallen in love with and yearned for him, and have become more like him because of that.

00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:30.830
Hmph, she’s just mimicking my way of speaking. How annoying.

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:34.660
Kinnosuke, you shouldn’t say such mean things.

00:04:34.660 --> 00:04:38.420
Come on, what’s wrong with going out on a date with me just once?

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:39.500
Stop bothering me!

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:41.500
If you’re going to get in the way of my work, get lost!

00:04:43.260 --> 00:04:46.880
What’s up with Kin-chan, getting all embarrassed and worked up...

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:52.100
That’s probably because Kinnosuke still only loves you.

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:53.850
That’s not true.

00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:56.730
I think he has some feelings for you.

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:58.350
Do you think so?

00:04:58.350 --> 00:04:59.980
Yeah, I’m sure!

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:06.580
But, I have to return to England soon.

00:05:08.530 --> 00:05:13.040
But, even so, if Kinnosuke tells me not to go back...

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:15.830
...then I plan on staying in Japan forever.

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:21.710
But, a person’s heart doesn’t always go the way you want it to.

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:24.000
It’ll be okay!

00:05:26.470 --> 00:05:28.380
I’ll help you.

00:05:28.380 --> 00:05:29.340
Help?

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:30.930
Leave it to me, Chris.

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:34.720
Code name: Kin-chan knock out super plan!

00:05:39.350 --> 00:05:40.770
Eh? Birthday party?

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:42.150
That’s right.

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:44.900
We’ve never done anything like that before, right?

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:47.400
That’s true, but my birthday is in two months.

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:49.240
Oh, was it?

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:51.370
Yep. December 29th.

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:56.330
Well, Satomi, Jinko and Chris will all be there to celebrate.

00:05:56.330 --> 00:05:58.790
Why are you doing this out of the blue? It’s strange.

00:05:58.790 --> 00:06:02.500
However, since you’re doing this celebration for me, I’d be happy to attend.

00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:05.500
That’s the way to approach it!

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:09.260
You’re going to come too, right, Irie-kun?

00:06:09.260 --> 00:06:11.720
There’s no way I’m going to something like that.

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:15.850
Besides, next week, I have an academic meeting with my professor,

00:06:15.850 --> 00:06:18.600
so I have a lot of preparation to do.

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:21.230
Academic meeting?
Even though you’re a student?

00:06:21.230 --> 00:06:22.900
Isn’t that really good?

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:24.480
No idea.

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:25.690
It’s definitely good!

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:30.700
Either way, you should stop interfering with other people’s feelings.

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:35.160
But, I want to support Chris...

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:36.370
Let her be.

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:40.460
People’s feelings will change when they do.

00:06:46.460 --> 00:06:49.460
Kinnosuke, happy birthday!

00:06:50.510 --> 00:06:52.970
Thank you, thank you!

00:06:56.930 --> 00:06:58.720
Sorry for the wait.

00:06:58.720 --> 00:07:00.140
We’ve been waiting.

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:02.310
Now, now, I’ll light the candles.

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:04.560
What a great cake!

00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:07.520
Ain’t it? Chris baked it.

00:07:08.150 --> 00:07:10.070
Oh, really?

00:07:10.070 --> 00:07:12.780
Kinnosuke, do you not like it?

00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:15.530
No, it’s not that. I don’t like sweet stuff.

00:07:15.530 --> 00:07:17.780
And it’s also a bit too flashy.

00:07:18.450 --> 00:07:19.870
Kin-chan!

00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:21.500
I got it.

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:23.080
I’m going to blow out the candles.

00:07:28.090 --> 00:07:29.840
Kin-chan, eat up!

00:07:33.550 --> 00:07:34.470
It’s good!

00:07:34.470 --> 00:07:35.300
Right?

00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:36.970
This captures the Japanese taste!

00:07:36.970 --> 00:07:38.350
Kotoko, you do know how to cook!

00:07:38.350 --> 00:07:40.350
Chris made that.

00:07:41.850 --> 00:07:44.020
Is it good, Kinnosuke?

00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:45.730
I’m so happy.

00:07:45.730 --> 00:07:47.440
It’s a fluke.

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:48.400
I have to try the others too.

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:53.360
It’s so spicy!

00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:56.030
See. That’s the extent of your abilities.

00:07:56.820 --> 00:07:59.080
I made that...

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:01.750
Really?

00:08:01.750 --> 00:08:05.170
So, do you have a better opinion of Chris now?

00:08:05.170 --> 00:08:09.090
She worked all day and night just for you.

00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:12.800
Oh, be quiet!

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:14.170
Kinnosuke.

00:08:14.170 --> 00:08:15.050
What is it?

00:08:15.050 --> 00:08:17.470
Your birthday present.

00:08:18.300 --> 00:08:20.970
Please accept it.

00:08:20.970 --> 00:08:22.020
What is this?

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:23.390
Kin-chan!

00:08:27.770 --> 00:08:29.480
A hand-knit sweater!

00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:31.940
It’s really well made!

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:36.150
I made a matching pair.

00:08:37.030 --> 00:08:41.450
I’m not very good at knitting, but I tried my best to knit it.

00:08:42.370 --> 00:08:44.000
Oh, Kin-chan is blushing.

00:08:44.910 --> 00:08:48.210
If you’re happy then just say that you’re happy.

00:08:48.210 --> 00:08:49.630
Shut up!

00:08:51.500 --> 00:08:52.880
What’s wrong with you all?!

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:54.630
Working up such a stupid scheme!

00:08:55.590 --> 00:08:56.840
Kin-chan...

00:08:56.840 --> 00:08:58.970
How many times do I have to tell you before you get it?!

00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:01.010
Kotoko is my only love!

00:09:02.010 --> 00:09:03.770
Kinnosuke?

00:09:04.430 --> 00:09:06.940
Who would ever wear this?!

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:12.320
You! Go back to England or America or where ever you came from now!

00:09:12.770 --> 00:09:13.820
Kin-chan...

00:09:17.650 --> 00:09:19.200
Very well.

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:26.960
Chris, wait!

00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:31.670
Thank you. Kotoko. Satomi. Jinko.

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:32.960
Goodbye...

00:09:38.380 --> 00:09:40.550
What’s she sulking about?

00:09:40.550 --> 00:09:42.180
That’s just too cruel, Kin-chan.

00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:44.010
It’s better to make a big deal of it.

00:09:44.010 --> 00:09:46.100
After all, she’ll be back to bother me again soon, right?

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:47.060
She won’t.

00:09:48.890 --> 00:09:52.060
Chris is going back to England.

00:09:54.020 --> 00:09:57.570
It was hard for her to part with you.

00:09:58.450 --> 00:10:00.700
She wanted you to like her.

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:03.280
She tried so hard, and yet...

00:10:03.830 --> 00:10:05.330
Kotoko.

00:10:05.830 --> 00:10:07.870
How could you say such things?!

00:10:07.870 --> 00:10:09.750
You’re an idiot, Kin-chan!

00:10:09.750 --> 00:10:11.170
Kotoko!

00:10:20.840 --> 00:10:22.180
Chris!

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:26.390
Chris, I’m sorry.

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:29.060
The birthday plan was a failure.

00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:31.400
It’s not your fault, Kotoko.

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:32.690
But...

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:38.780
I wanted to become Japanese.

00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:43.160
I wanted to become Japanese...

00:10:45.870 --> 00:10:47.290
Chris!

00:10:56.460 --> 00:10:58.710
Sheesh. I told you so.

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:04.510
Besides, there’s never been an instance where your plans worked.

00:11:05.390 --> 00:11:07.060
What’s wrong?

00:11:07.970 --> 00:11:10.640
Well, my stomach doesn’t feel so good.

00:11:10.640 --> 00:11:13.350
Wasn’t it because you were crying while drowning your sorrows with food?

00:11:17.780 --> 00:11:19.030
Are you all right?

00:11:20.440 --> 00:11:22.030
You have a slight fever.

00:11:22.490 --> 00:11:23.950
Open your mouth.

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:27.280
It’s not inflamed.

00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:30.290
You’re really like a doctor.

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:36.790
If it gets any worse, then go to the hospital tomorrow to get some medicine.

00:11:38.920 --> 00:11:40.050
Have a safe trip.

00:11:40.510 --> 00:11:42.130
Don’t overwork yourself today.

00:11:42.130 --> 00:11:43.050
Yes.

00:11:47.300 --> 00:11:49.140
Kotoko-chan, is there something wrong with you?

00:11:49.140 --> 00:11:53.480
It’s no biggie. I just have a slight fever and a bit of nausea.

00:11:53.480 --> 00:11:55.600
What did you just say?

00:11:56.360 --> 00:11:57.440
Do you have nausea?

00:11:57.440 --> 00:11:58.860
Yes.

00:11:58.860 --> 00:12:00.650
And a slight fever too, right?

00:12:00.650 --> 00:12:01.690
Yes.

00:12:01.690 --> 00:12:02.860
How about your period?

00:12:02.860 --> 00:12:04.950
It’s a little late...

00:12:04.950 --> 00:12:08.660
Could it be? No! It has to be!

00:12:08.660 --> 00:12:10.160
What’s wrong?

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:12.750
It’s gonna get real busy here.

00:12:13.750 --> 00:12:14.960
Mother?

00:12:17.540 --> 00:12:19.170
Chris.

00:12:19.170 --> 00:12:20.670
Hello?

00:12:20.670 --> 00:12:23.470
Kotoko, thank you for everything.

00:12:23.470 --> 00:12:27.140
I’m going back to England on today’s flight.

00:12:27.140 --> 00:12:28.600
Wait, Chris!

00:12:35.860 --> 00:12:37.150
Hey, are you all right?

00:12:37.150 --> 00:12:40.360
I’m sorry, I’ll clean it right away.

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:44.410
Kinnosuke, what’s wrong with you today?

00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:46.330
It’s nothing.

00:12:46.330 --> 00:12:47.660
Hello, Kin-chan?

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:50.500
There’s a problem! Chris is going back home!

00:12:50.950 --> 00:12:54.120
Chris will be going back home on today’s flight!

00:12:54.120 --> 00:12:55.320
What are you saying?

00:12:55.320 --> 00:12:56.420
Get here now!

00:12:58.300 --> 00:12:59.920
It’s impossible. I can’t go.

00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:01.490
Kin-chan?

00:13:01.490 --> 00:13:04.260
I’m going to prepare the shop now.

00:13:04.260 --> 00:13:06.230
You’re never going to see her again if you leave it like this!

00:13:06.230 --> 00:13:07.890
That’s right. So what?

00:13:07.890 --> 00:13:10.140
Just let her be if she wants to go back.

00:13:10.140 --> 00:13:12.560
How do you expect me to go when you’ve just told me today?

00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:13.690
Kin-chan!

00:13:13.690 --> 00:13:15.350
I’m busy, so I’m going to hang up.

00:13:21.240 --> 00:13:28.450
The number you have called is currently out of service range or is currently switched off.

00:13:29.740 --> 00:13:32.410
Geez, what the heck Kin-chan doing?!

00:13:32.410 --> 00:13:33.910
It’s okay.

00:13:35.250 --> 00:13:37.080
No, it’s not! Because...!

00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:38.130
Kotoko.

00:13:38.920 --> 00:13:41.630
I’ve been under your care for such a long time.

00:13:41.630 --> 00:13:47.180
The nine o’clock bus for Narita Airport will be departing momentarily.

00:13:47.180 --> 00:13:49.640
Passengers, please board immediately.

00:13:49.640 --> 00:13:51.270
Well, I’m going.

00:13:52.640 --> 00:13:55.600
Sheesh, what are you doing, Kin-chan?

00:13:55.600 --> 00:13:57.190
We’re departing momentarily.

00:13:57.190 --> 00:13:59.060
I’m going too!

00:13:59.060 --> 00:14:00.520
Closing the door.

00:14:03.990 --> 00:14:05.280
Hey, Kinnosuke.

00:14:05.280 --> 00:14:07.280
Huh? What is it?

00:14:07.280 --> 00:14:08.910
Look below.

00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:14.460
You’re acting strangely today.

00:14:14.460 --> 00:14:16.290
I’m sorry.

00:14:16.710 --> 00:14:19.630
She flies at twelve, got it?

00:14:19.630 --> 00:14:21.710
Make sure you’re not late!

00:14:23.550 --> 00:14:26.760
Thank you. Kotoko. Satomi. Jinko.

00:14:26.760 --> 00:14:28.140
Goodbye...

00:14:36.020 --> 00:14:38.480
Your birthday present.

00:14:38.480 --> 00:14:40.400
...matching pair...

00:14:43.610 --> 00:14:45.280
Today...

00:14:45.280 --> 00:14:46.240
Boss!

00:14:46.240 --> 00:14:47.530
What is it?

00:14:48.200 --> 00:14:49.030
I’m sorry.

00:14:50.120 --> 00:14:52.160
But, please let me leave for today!

00:14:52.160 --> 00:14:53.330
Hey, Kinnosuke!

00:14:54.120 --> 00:14:55.490
Where are you going?

00:14:55.490 --> 00:14:57.750
Hey, Kinnosuke!

00:14:59.580 --> 00:15:05.590
The 12:00 British Airlines flight for Heathrow Airport, London, is now calling.

00:15:05.590 --> 00:15:06.380
Kotoko.

00:15:06.380 --> 00:15:08.220
The 12:00 British Airlines flight for Heathrow Airport, London, is now calling.

00:15:09.510 --> 00:15:12.760
I really had a lot of fun in Japan.

00:15:12.760 --> 00:15:14.930
I’m counting on you to pass my message to Kinnosuke.

00:15:16.480 --> 00:15:17.390
Chris...

00:15:18.020 --> 00:15:21.690
Well then, Kotoko. This is really goodbye.

00:15:22.770 --> 00:15:23.980
Chris!

00:15:27.070 --> 00:15:32.280
To be honest, I wanted to see Kinnosuke once more.

00:15:33.330 --> 00:15:35.490
But, this is bye-bye.

00:15:49.760 --> 00:15:50.590
Kin-chan!

00:15:51.760 --> 00:15:54.430
You’re late, Kin-chan! What were you doing?

00:15:57.220 --> 00:15:58.100
Where’s Chris?

00:15:58.100 --> 00:15:59.390
She already left.

00:15:59.390 --> 00:16:01.060
What did you say? Which way?

00:16:03.440 --> 00:16:05.520
Damn it! That idiot!

00:16:05.520 --> 00:16:06.780
Kin-chan?

00:16:12.780 --> 00:16:13.950
Kotoko.

00:16:14.830 --> 00:16:15.530
I’m sorry.

00:16:17.290 --> 00:16:18.450
Chris!

00:16:19.040 --> 00:16:20.460
Wait, Chris!

00:16:20.460 --> 00:16:21.460
Stop!

00:16:21.460 --> 00:16:22.630
Let me through!

00:16:22.630 --> 00:16:23.880
Your ticket!

00:16:23.880 --> 00:16:25.420
Shut up! I don’t have one!

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:27.500
You can’t go past here!

00:16:27.500 --> 00:16:30.170
Let me go! Let me go, will you!

00:16:30.170 --> 00:16:31.510
Kin-chan!

00:16:32.340 --> 00:16:33.680
You two!

00:16:33.680 --> 00:16:34.850
Kin-chan, go!

00:16:34.850 --> 00:16:36.140
Sorry, Kotoko.

00:16:36.140 --> 00:16:38.140
Chris! Where are you?!

00:16:38.140 --> 00:16:39.480
Stop!

00:16:39.480 --> 00:16:40.600
Come here!

00:16:40.600 --> 00:16:41.640
Chris!

00:16:41.640 --> 00:16:43.480
Calm down!
Come back!

00:16:43.480 --> 00:16:45.310
Can’t you hear me? You idiot!

00:16:45.310 --> 00:16:47.730
I’m wearing the sweater you knit!

00:16:47.730 --> 00:16:49.860
Please, come and see!

00:16:49.860 --> 00:16:51.280
Please stop struggling.

00:16:51.280 --> 00:16:53.950
What’s with you? Let me go, you idiots!

00:16:53.950 --> 00:16:55.030
Please calm down!

00:16:55.030 --> 00:16:57.580
Chris, come back!

00:16:57.580 --> 00:17:00.290
Because, I’ve grown to love you a little!

00:17:00.290 --> 00:17:02.870
Stay in Japan!

00:17:02.870 --> 00:17:06.670
Chris! Come back!

00:17:14.130 --> 00:17:15.300
Kin-chan...

00:17:19.470 --> 00:17:20.560
Chris...

00:17:20.560 --> 00:17:22.230
Good morning, Kinnosuke!

00:17:25.480 --> 00:17:26.810
Why are you...?

00:17:27.610 --> 00:17:30.690
I was thinking of returning home...

00:17:30.690 --> 00:17:34.820
...but your face kept floating in my head, so I just couldn’t take it any more.

00:17:34.820 --> 00:17:37.200
So, I got them to let me off the plane.

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:39.200
Umm, Chris...

00:17:39.990 --> 00:17:41.290
What is it?

00:17:41.290 --> 00:17:45.170
So, you didn’t come back because you heard Kin-chan’s voice...?

00:17:45.170 --> 00:17:47.750
Did you say something, Kinnosuke?

00:17:47.750 --> 00:17:50.670
No, I didn’t. Forget it.

00:17:51.630 --> 00:17:53.550
Wait, Kinnosuke!

00:17:53.550 --> 00:17:56.090
I know very well that I’m nothing but trouble for you.

00:17:56.090 --> 00:17:56.970
Let go.

00:17:56.970 --> 00:18:00.980
That may be so, but I’ll keep attacking until your feelings change!

00:18:10.110 --> 00:18:12.360
Kotoko, I’ll try my best!

00:18:15.490 --> 00:18:17.200
Do your best, Chris!

00:18:17.200 --> 00:18:18.410
I will!

00:18:21.120 --> 00:18:22.370
I’m home!

00:18:22.950 --> 00:18:25.660
Geez, where have you been, Kotoko-chan?

00:18:30.420 --> 00:18:33.050
Umm, mother, what could this be?

00:18:33.050 --> 00:18:34.840
Can’t you tell by looking?

00:18:34.840 --> 00:18:36.380
They’re baby products!

00:18:36.380 --> 00:18:39.800
I just couldn’t take it any more!

00:18:39.800 --> 00:18:43.560
Kotoko-chan, this may be jumping the gun a little though.

00:18:45.270 --> 00:18:47.940
Kotoko-chan, you’re pregnant.

00:18:47.940 --> 00:18:49.440
Huh?! Me?!

00:18:49.440 --> 00:18:52.020
Come, we’re going to have a party tonight!

00:18:52.020 --> 00:18:55.820
And this is a dish made especially for expecting mothers.

00:18:55.820 --> 00:18:58.570
I was thinking of delivering this to the neighbors too.

00:18:58.570 --> 00:19:00.570
Aww, Aihara-san.

00:19:02.080 --> 00:19:04.280
I have a baby inside me?

00:19:04.280 --> 00:19:09.290
That’s right. I’m sure since I’ve given birth to two children myself.

00:19:12.000 --> 00:19:15.050
Irie-kun’s and my baby...

00:19:24.470 --> 00:19:25.850
What’s this commotion about?

00:19:25.850 --> 00:19:28.440
Irie-kun, weren’t you coming home tomorrow?

00:19:28.440 --> 00:19:30.190
Well, today...

00:19:30.190 --> 00:19:33.480
Come on now, Kotoko-chan. You have some news to tell him, right?

00:19:35.530 --> 00:19:38.070
It’s seems that I’m pregnant.

00:19:38.070 --> 00:19:39.320
Is that true?!

00:19:40.070 --> 00:19:40.990
Probably.

00:19:40.990 --> 00:19:42.620
Probably? And the doctor?

00:19:43.240 --> 00:19:45.160
I haven’t gone to see one yet.

00:19:46.410 --> 00:19:48.410
I think we can still make it now.

00:19:52.840 --> 00:19:54.130
What a handsome man.

00:19:54.130 --> 00:19:55.840
How dreamy.

00:19:55.840 --> 00:19:57.720
I wonder who his wife is.

00:19:57.720 --> 00:19:59.050
How lucky.

00:20:03.890 --> 00:20:06.260
Irie-kun, I...

00:20:06.260 --> 00:20:08.100
They said I had an inflamed stomach...

00:20:08.770 --> 00:20:10.480
So, they were wrong.

00:20:11.440 --> 00:20:14.150
I’m sorry! I guessed incorrectly!

00:20:14.150 --> 00:20:17.400
Geez, it’s because you jumped the gun without first visiting the doctor.

00:20:17.400 --> 00:20:20.360
Well, this time, it was my mother’s fault.

00:20:20.360 --> 00:20:23.700
What should I tell them?

00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:27.620
If you’re not pregnant, then you’re not.
There’s no helping it.

00:20:27.620 --> 00:20:30.790
Besides, how were your results?

00:20:31.370 --> 00:20:33.330
The results came out today, right?

00:20:36.170 --> 00:20:37.460
What are you doing?

00:20:37.460 --> 00:20:39.800
Wait.

00:20:39.800 --> 00:20:43.510
What is it now? The results are right there.

00:20:43.510 --> 00:20:46.390
I know, but I’m not mentally prepared!

00:20:50.060 --> 00:20:52.060
What is it? What was that “Ah” about?

00:20:56.110 --> 00:20:57.440
It’s there!

00:20:59.690 --> 00:21:01.150
What’s wrong?

00:21:01.150 --> 00:21:03.450
I feel my strength sapped after being overcome with relief.

00:21:03.450 --> 00:21:05.280
Geez, you’re so hopeless.

00:21:05.780 --> 00:21:06.870
Come on, let’s go.

00:21:06.870 --> 00:21:08.410
Where to?

00:21:11.170 --> 00:21:13.540
I was supposed to take you out on a date if you passed, right?

00:21:15.380 --> 00:21:16.790
Thank you, Irie-kun!

00:21:17.290 --> 00:21:18.590
How annoying.

00:21:18.590 --> 00:21:22.880
Could it be that you came back early because of this?

00:21:23.760 --> 00:21:24.760
Something like that.

00:21:24.760 --> 00:21:26.010
I’m so happy!

00:21:26.010 --> 00:21:28.680
Sheesh. So, where do you want to go?

00:21:29.890 --> 00:21:32.440
Onii-chan and Kotoko-chan sure are late.

00:21:32.440 --> 00:21:34.600
My first grandchild!

00:23:07.490 --> 00:23:10.780
Hey, Jinko, did you hear? Kotoko passed the nursing exam!

00:23:10.780 --> 00:23:14.750
Really? I’m gonna make Kotoko the model of hope for my life after all.

00:23:14.750 --> 00:23:17.070
Is that willpower your tribute to her?

00:23:17.070 --> 00:23:19.800
Ah, the Nursing Section’s got plenty of hot guys!

00:23:19.800 --> 00:23:22.330
By the way, Satomi, are we...

00:23:22.330 --> 00:23:25.540
...going to have... any more scenes?!

00:23:26.350 --> 00:23:28.460
Next time on Itazura na Kiss:

00:23:28.460 --> 00:23:30.420
Enviable new face!?

00:23:30.420 --> 00:23:32.300
I’m definitely gonna be happy.
